config UHC_XHCI_ALIF
	bool "Alif Ensemble xHCI USB host controller driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_ALIF_XHCI_UHC_ENABLED
	depends on UHC_DRIVER
	help
	  xHCI USB-2.0 host driver for the Alif Ensemble USB (DWC3-family,
	  controller base 0x48200000, IRQ 101).

	  Implements the full uhc_api: DWC3 host-mode init + xHCI reset,
	  command/event-ring processing, root-hub port reset + single-device
	  enumeration, ep_enqueue/ep_dequeue (control/bulk/interrupt), bus
	  reset/suspend/resume, disable/shutdown, and an event-ring IRQ for
	  hotplug notification.

	  Bring-up through *_enable()/enumerate() was proven on an E8 EVK
	  (see the timing comments in uhc_xhci_alif_first_light()). Later
	  additions (ep_enqueue/ep_dequeue, bus suspend/resume, disable/
	  shutdown, the ISR) follow the same register sequencing but have
	  NOT themselves been bench-run -- see issue #388 for the open bench
	  checklist, including the EVK's own D+/D- signal-path fix needed
	  before end-to-end enumeration of a real device can be proven.

	  Driver: zephyr/drivers/usb/uhc/uhc_xhci_alif.c
	  Binding: zephyr/dts/bindings/usb/alif,xhci-uhc.yaml
